__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
tools/ui-smoke/pwenv/
frontend-v2/node_modules/

# internal working notes — never published. `docs/*` rather than `docs/` so the
# one shipped guide can be re-included below: a file inside an excluded
# DIRECTORY cannot be re-included, no matter what the negation says.
docs/*
# the agent-integration guide is user-facing documentation, not a working note —
# it is shipped in the wheel/repo and pointed at from the legacy UI.
!docs/AGENTS.md
# docs/design/ is the other exception: an engineering SPECIFICATION is a
# deliverable that a reviewer, a future maintainer and CI all have to be able to
# read, not a working note that only exists on one machine. `!docs/design/`
# re-includes the directory (which `docs/*` excluded) so git descends into it;
# without that first line the second cannot work, because a file inside an
# excluded DIRECTORY can never be re-included.
!docs/design/
!docs/design/**
